    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61240" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλῐκ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.6
				</span></i>
			) <i>suffering in the colon, having colic</i>, prob.l. in <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.40
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κ. διάθεσις</span>
			<i>colic</i>, from its being seated in the colon and parts
			adjacent, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				8.384
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. φάρμακα</span> remedies
				<i>for colic</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				13.266
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἀντίδοτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Androm.
				</span></i>
			 ap. eund.<i><span class="en">
				13.276
			</span></i>. Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					19.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
